From 3215c318b16f932f29e4b11c6253a5f5371031af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 23:49:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] flow-iosched: apply three-phase structural audit fixes (v3.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1 — Critical data-safety fixes:
  C-1: Merge rbtree corruption on non-mergeable dispatch is fixed by
       guarding elv_rb_del in flow_remove_request with the same
       rq_mergeable condition used at insertion. The old wrapper
       flow_del_from_merge_rb relied on RB_EMPTY_NODE which returns
       false for freshly kmem_cache_alloc'd (zeroed) nodes, causing
       rb_erase to corrupt the merge tree root.
  C-2: Added flow_depth_updated callback and registered it in the
       elevator ops. Without this, nr_requests changes at runtime
       left the async depth throttle permanently stale.
  C-3: flow_limit_depth now uses blk_mq_is_sync_read(opf) instead of
       op_is_sync(opf) && !op_is_write(opf), matching the established
       kernel pattern used by mq-deadline and kyber.
  H-4: Added flow_requeue_request handler that returns consumed budget
       sectors on requeue. Without this, requeued I/O caused budget
       leaks and spurious containment.

Phase 2 — Correctness hardening:
  H-5: Autotune timer now holds fd->lock for all tuned_starvation_max
       writes, eliminating the data race between the I/O path
       (flow_starved_lane under fd->lock) and the timer. The old
       READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE hacks are removed.
  H-6/H-7: flow_exit_hctx now completes pending requests with
       BLK_STS_IOERR instead of silently discarding them. flow_has_work
       now NULL-checks khd before dereferencing.
  M-8: dl_group allocations now use a mempool (dl_group_pool) instead
       of raw kmem_cache_zalloc, guaranteeing forward progress up to
       q->nr_requests concurrent allocations.

Phase 3 — Structural re-architecture:
  Reduced from 5 lanes (Emergency/Reserved/Latency/Shared/Contained)
  to 4 lanes (Emergency/Read/Write/Contained). The old Latency and
  Reserved lanes are merged into a single Read lane, and Shared is
  renamed to Write. This eliminates the scx_flow-derived IO profile
  recomputation, latency credit/debt system, and per-hctx dispatch-
  list fast path — none of which added measurable benefit over the
  simpler design and each introduced data-safety risk.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 block/Kconfig.iosched |  23 +-
 block/flow-iosched.c  | 577 +++++++++++++++++++-----------------------
 2 files changed, 271 insertions(+), 329 deletions(-)

